# proto-file: humanoid_nmpc/humanoid_rerun_viewer/proto/plot_config.proto
# proto-message: humanoid_rerun_viewer_proto.PlotConfig
#
# The default plot configuration for humanoid_rerun_viewer.
#
# Configured signals can be:
# - Full tab titles (e.g. "Base Pose & Euler", "Joint Dynamics")
# - Panel titles (e.g. "Base Pos X [m]", "Left Foot Normal Force Fz [N]")
# - Telemetry paths or wildcards (e.g. "base_pose/*", "contact_forces/left_normal", "joints/position/*")
# - Status paths or series (e.g. "status/mpc/*", "status/robot/loop_period", "MPC Solve Time [ms]")
# - Custom telemetry paths (placed into custom_tab_title, default "Signals")
#
# Configured 3D robot visualizations:
# - robot_instances: "measured", "terminal_state", "terminal_target" (default: every instance the scene carries)
# - draw_terminal_state: false draws only "measured" (no end-of-trajectory robots, whatever robot_instances says), as
#   this file does; --terminal_state on the bridge brings them back
#
# The MuJoCo viewer of the robot process, which reads it from its plot configuration unless a viewer is named
# (make launch-<robot>-sim: PLOT_CONFIG=, default this directory's plot_config.textproto; VIEWER= names one):
# LINT.IfChange(default_mujoco_viewer)
# - mujoco_viewer: "web" (a browser tab at http://localhost:6090), "glfw" (a window on DISPLAY) or "none"; repeated, a
#   preference list tried in order: mujoco_viewer: ["web", "none"] runs without a viewer where the web viewer cannot
#   start (default: "web")
# LINT.ThenChange(//humanoid_nmpc/humanoid_common_mpc_app/robot/include/humanoid_common_mpc_app/robot/RobotAppOptions.h:default_viewer)

signals: "Base Pose & Euler"
signals: "contact_forces/*"
signals: "joints/position/measured"
signals: "status/mpc/solve_time"
custom_tab_title: "Signals"
draw_terminal_state: false
mujoco_viewer: "web"
